if there's one thing all super mario  games have in common it's the massive  amounts of creative platforming and  funny characters that make for the truly  unforgettable adventures that many of us  hold near and dear to our hearts  if there are two things they have in  common it's the many features that were  going to be in the games but got cut  from the final game before release  no joke there are literally so many  hidden items  areas animations and even complete game  function to be found in the game's files  that the hardest part of writing this  script was actually just choosing the  few most  interesting features to talk about you  know so this video doesn't end up being  2 hours long  and since we had the big data leak  recently from super mario 64 which i'm  sure  many of you have heard about i'm  actually not going to cover 64 in this  video  but rest assured i have delved through  the pages and pages of hidden and cut  content from super mario sunshine and  super mario galaxy  so that i could bring this freshly baked  cake of interesting information to your  youtube watch page for your viewing  pleasure  and what's more is this video was so big  that i have been gracefully joined by a  fabulous fellow youtuber to help bring  it to life  please welcome the one and only nintendo  black crisis from the channel nintendo  black  crisis well since we have two games to  cover in this one let's start off with  the newer one  super mario galaxy as many of you will  recall the game takes the classic super  mario platforming experience and throws  it  to infinity and beyond  you spend a lot of the time running  around different worlds i mean  galaxies that each have a bunch of  different little planets for mario to  run around on  and i mean a bunch but speaking of  planets  the game was actually supposed to  feature a lot more some of which  are pretty interesting we've got cut  planets like the star planet which is  just a giant power star from mario 64.  bathtub planet which is a giant bathtub  home planet which was actually used for  some demo pictures before the game's  release  and a planet shaped like a giant disc  with its own clouds and sun  but of all the removed planets the most  interesting one is definitely the  starman fort planet  which was actually fully developed and  caused the development team a bit of  heartache when it was scrapped  according to this concept art starman  fort was actually the first planet  designed for the game and  even helped to solidify the super mario  game as super mario galaxy  we can't know for sure why this was  scrapped ultimately  maybe it was because it didn't fit with  the story somehow but either way it's  very interesting that the first planet  that was fully designed and developed  and that helped give life to the entire  game is something nobody will ever get  to experience by normal means  and that's kind of depressing well how  about we look at some removed models and  animations to lighten things up  as is commonly found in the game files  of games that were developed by teams  who develop  multiple games there are actually models  embedded in galaxy from the team's  previous projects like this boat from  super mario sunshine or some  enemies from donkey kong jungle beat no  joke  although these models were most likely  never actually intended to be in the  game and were probably  added in just for some testing early on  in development but  some enemy models definitely were like  these bullies from mario 64 that were  fully modeled and textured and even  animated there's also this strange  little enemy called a canopy which is a  play on toad's japanese name  kenopio and you can see why it's got  this strange  drawn on looking face and apparently was  animated to hop around and harm mario if  he touched it  and to be honest with you i'm not sure  whether to be terrified of the thing or  to find it  strangely adorable but speaking of  animations mario himself  actually has an entire set of animations  cut from the game  and wouldn't you know it they're all  related to playing tennis  yeah tennis in space we've got stuff  like running with a tennis racket  hitting with a tennis racket even  waiting  with a tennis racket i have no idea  where or how this would have been  implemented into the game but my guess  is this idea was scrapped to make way  for the standalone tennis title  mario tennis aces which is  understandable since they did do a whole  lot with that concept and it was  probably way too big to fit into a super  mario title  the last bit of cut models i'll cover  for galaxy would be these interesting  looking vehicles  one that resembles large legs called the  two leg walker  and the other that resembles a tiny  two-wheeled car called the two-wheel  tank  both vehicles were apparently scrapped  even before receiving textures but i'd  imagine that they would change the way  some of the terrain or even enemies felt  let's move on to super mario sunshine  which has even more cut content than  galaxy did  since the release of super mario 3d  all-stars no doubt  many of you have heard the really choppy  voice editing that happens when mario  picks up flood for the first time  i mean even though it's understandable  since it would have probably been a huge  hassle to get the voice actress  kit harris back for the re-release of  the game just to record those few lines  it's still kind of jarring to listen to  since flood now tells you to press the  button over and over  use the button to press the button you  can then press the button  to enter a body of water and press the  button  but speaking of voice lines mario  actually has quite a few that were cut  from the games released back in 2002  and i mean actual lines not just random  yahoos or yippies  for longtime fans of the mario series or  nintendo games in general  you probably know that a pretty common  trend in nintendo games is for the  protagonists to not audibly speak  much or in some cases at all looking at  you  zelda this is the same when it comes to  mario but apparently the initial plan  was to have mario talk quite a bit more  in sunshine  here have a listen ciao another door  hello door primo cool too  cool perfecting it's fun feeling good  oh my head i imagine you'll be spending  a fair amount of time at the princess's  side  hmm look like a mario's gonna have to  find a job  that last line the one about mario  finding a job is quite funny since i'm  pretty sure the whole plumbing gig  is just a cover up he's clearly a  professional mustache grower  but the self-referential humor is only  present in the japanese version of the  game  even though it was recorded in english  definitely  doesn't make sense as to why it was  removed for the international versions  but who knows maybe the developers  figured mario shouldn't be heard talking  about getting a job because then  we would get jobs and stop playing mario  games as much  but enough about mario's voice lines  let's talk about removed objects and  models  there's an unused enemy called the  hinokiri which literally translates to  fire chestnut  hence its fiery chestnut-like appearance  this enemy can be seen in the space  world 2001 trailer for sunshine but was  cut  by the time the game actually released  though its files still can be found  there's also a removed nozzle for flood  that was never  actually modeled but had its mechanics  built into the empty game object that  was  apparently going to be a sniper nozzle  the sniper was going to be able to shoot  water at 100 times the power of the  regular nozzle  after a charge up period similar to the  rocket nozzle  which we're assuming is what the nozzle  evolved into  not that i was able to use any of those  for my sunshine challenge video  there are also some removed areas for  the game and a giant  cut mechanic that i have no clue how it  would have been used had it not gotten  cut from the final release  but let's start with the areas i'm sure  many of you are all too familiar with  the trend of placing a giant eel in a  super mario water level  and in sunshine not only do we have to  descend deep under the water triggering  everyone's thalassophobia into some  ancient submerged ruins but we do so  to fight a giant eel or rather to brush  its teeth lots of fans have  very very vivid memories of this boss  fight but there's actually a detail  regarding the eel that implies that  there may have been another mechanic to  this fight you see the eel's throat and  stomach  are not only modeled but fully textured  as well  meaning the eel was probably initially  meant to you know  swallow you whole for those of you who  have played the legend of zelda ocarina  of time  being swallowed by sea creatures is  apparently a trend with nintendo games  but enough about jonah and the giant eel  delving once again into the cut content  from sunshine there are several  references and commands and even camera  behaviors that allude to the inclusion  of  multiplayer in the game yeah multiplayer  and what's even more  crazy is it apparently wasn't going to  be the kind of multiplayer that we see  in odyssey  where another player can control the  gadget feature while the first player  controls mario as far as i can tell the  second player was actually going to  control  shadow mario this functionality was  probably scrapped early on since  trying to access it makes the camera  super glitchy but my guess  is that one player was supposed to be  mario hosing down the other player  playing as shadow mario which may have  actually been a pretty neat multiplayer  idea now that i'm thinking about it  but alas this and many other minor  features will never be experienced by  anyone through normal means and the  multiplayer is  too broken to ever experience without a  complete recreation from the ground up  while there are quite a few other random  pieces of cut content in easter eggs  here and there i feel like we covered  the vast majority of the most  interesting ones and we'll end it there  but i wanted to include a big shout out  to the website that provided me with  more than 90  of the information from this video  called the cutting room floor it's a  place run by some passionate gaming  enthusiasts who love  delving in and finding content like this  and i wanted to give credit where credit  is due  so if any of the website's staff happens  to catch this video here's a big thank  you from the bandit  and also a huge thanks to nbc for  helping out with this video  really gave it that special flavoring it  needed be sure to catch the big sunshine  challenge video live  right now over on his channel featuring  yours truly where i contributed a  hundred percent of my vocals but  zero percent of the skill if you enjoyed  this video i would greatly appreciate it  if you would consider dropping a like so  youtube  knows it's a good video and subscribing  to the channel to stick around for the  next one  also huge huge huge thanks to all of my  supporters who help make  every video come to life in ways you  can't even imagine  if you're interested in joining the  ranks of my elite and getting some  pretty awesome perks along the way click  that join button below or follow the  links in the description to find out how  also down there are links to my social  media pages so come hang out over there  that's all i've got for this one so as  always i hope you have a wonderful rest  of your day  this is madintina bandit signing out  [Music]  you

